[TITLE:e200z4 Manual Extracted Findings - Validation Results]

[INTRO]
This document contains information extracted from the e200z4 Core Reference Manual
for validation against LLVM implementation. Manual available at:
https://www.elektronikjk.com/elementy_czynne/IC/E200Z4.pdf

[FIXES-APPLIED]
UID: FIXES-001

FIX_001: Corrected SPE instruction terminology
File: llvm/lib/Target/PowerPC/PPCScheduleE200Z4.td:226-228
Issue: Comment incorrectly said "must use ALU0" (e200z7 terminology) instead of DIS0 (e200z4 terminology)
Fix: Updated comment to use correct e200z4 dispatch port terminology (DIS0)
Status: ✓ FIXED

FIX_002: Added dual-issue pairing rules documentation
File: llvm/lib/Target/PowerPC/PPCScheduleE200Z4.td:275-302
Issue: Missing documentation about dual-issue pairing rules and incomplete model status
Fix: Added comprehensive comments documenting:
  - Need to extract pairing rules from manual Chapter 4
  - Known restrictions (SPE cannot pair, SU0-only instructions)
  - TODO items for complete model validation
Status: ✓ FIXED

FIX_003: Added FPR and SPEFSCR save logic for interrupt handlers
Files: 
  - llvm/lib/Target/PowerPC/PPCFrameLowering.cpp:1947-1984
  - llvm/lib/Target/PowerPC/PPCMachineFunctionInfo.h:83-91, 208-212
Issue: Interrupt handlers with SPE/FPU support (e200z4, e200z7) were not saving FPRs or SPEFSCR
Fix: Added logic to:
  - Detect FPR usage in interrupt handlers
  - Mark MustSaveFPRs flag when FPRs are used
  - Mark MustSaveSPEFSCR flag for SPE-enabled cores (e200z4, e200z7)
  - Added getter/setter methods to PPCMachineFunctionInfo
Status: ✓ FIXED (partial - prologue/epilogue code generation for FPR/SPEFSCR save still needed)

[CRITICAL-FINDINGS]
UID: CRITICAL

FINDING_001:
Issue: SPE instructions comment says "must use ALU0" but e200z4 uses SU0/DIS0 terminology
Code_Location: PPCScheduleE200Z4.td:226
Impact: Terminology mismatch may indicate incorrect understanding
Action: ✓ FIXED - Updated comment to use DIS0 terminology

FINDING_002:
Issue: No explicit SU0-only restrictions modeled in itineraries
Code_Location: PPCScheduleE200Z4.td:35-45
Impact: Scheduler may incorrectly allow SU1 for SU0-only instructions
Status: ⚠ NEEDS MANUAL EXTRACTION - Need to extract SU0-only instruction list from manual Chapter 4

FINDING_003:
Issue: Dual-issue pairing rules not explicitly modeled
Code_Location: PPCScheduleE200Z4.td:274-286
Impact: CompleteModel = 0, scheduler doesn't enforce pairing rules
Status: ⚠ NEEDS MANUAL EXTRACTION - Need pairing rules table from manual Chapter 4
Action: ✓ DOCUMENTED - Added comments explaining need for extraction

FINDING_004:
Issue: Interrupt context save doesn't handle SPRs, FPRs, SPEFSCR
Code_Location: PPCFrameLowering.cpp:1843-1913
Impact: Interrupt handlers corrupting register state for SPE/FPU operations
Status: ✓ PARTIALLY FIXED
  - Added FPR usage detection (lines 1947-1984)
  - Added MustSaveFPRs flag support
  - Added MustSaveSPEFSCR flag support
  - TODO: Implement actual save/restore code generation in emitPrologue/emitEpilogue

